TABLE OF CONTENTS

mcontainer/CloseContainer
mcontainer/OpenContainer
mcontainer/ReadContainerPacket
mcontainer/SeekContainer
mcontainer/CloseContainer                            mcontainer/CloseContainer

   NAME
	CloseContainer -- What the module holds of the file given back, if it made anything: after a failed open too.

   SYNOPSIS
	    void CloseContainer(*mcontainer.MediaContainerFile file)

   BEHAVIOR
	The file and its tracks' buffers stay the library's.
mcontainer/OpenContainer                              mcontainer/OpenContainer

   NAME
	OpenContainer -- The file's index read, its tracks and tags made out of it, and every track at its first packet: 0, or MERR_*.

   SYNOPSIS
	    i32 OpenContainer(*mcontainer.MediaContainerFile file, bool check)

   BEHAVIOR
	With `check`, MERR_UNKNOWN when the bytes are not its kind's. On what
	opened the file, which it reads.
mcontainer/ReadContainerPacket                  mcontainer/ReadContainerPacket

   NAME
	ReadContainerPacket -- The track's next packet into `packet`: 0, MERR_END, or MERR_*.

   SYNOPSIS
	    i32 ReadContainerPacket(*mcontainer.MediaContainerFile file, u32 track, *media.MediaPacket packet)

   BEHAVIOR
	Its bytes are in the track's buffer, good until the track's next read or
	seek.
mcontainer/SeekContainer                              mcontainer/SeekContainer

   NAME
	SeekContainer -- The track moved to the key packet at or before `time`, in microseconds: 0, or MERR_*.

   SYNOPSIS
	    i32 SeekContainer(*mcontainer.MediaContainerFile file, u32 track, i64 time)

   BEHAVIOR
	The file can seek; `track` is one it has.
